    "set2-l1-q21-22": {
      "scriptHash": "6725c17bc461973b117c4f8af70105c92cdb3a460aadab7667e41a001db8194c",
      "sigVersion": 3,
      "bytes": 611100,
      "durationSec": 38.13,
      "audioSha256": "cefbd11c29ad03c943d0a00bda3b247e5d48428d14f5d9b1135484218b5292cf",
      "stt": {
        "verdict": "PASS",
        "wer": 0.0119,
        "backend": "faster_whisper",
        "reason": "WER 1.2%",
        "transcript": "For those interested in teaching, the Graduate School of Education is accepting applications for its Teaching Assistant Training Program. This semester-long program covers classroom management, lesson planning, and effective communication strategies. Participants will observe experienced instructors and conduct supervised teaching sessions. Upon completion, you'll receive a certificate recognized by departments across campus. Open up at the Education Building, Office 210, and submit a one-page statement describing your teaching goals along with one faculty reference letter. Applications close in two weeks.",
        "audioSha256": "cefbd11c29ad03c943d0a00bda3b247e5d48428d14f5d9b1135484218b5292cf",
        "scriptHash": "6725c17bc461973b117c4f8af70105c92cdb3a460aadab7667e41a001db8194c"
      }
    },
    "set2-l1-q23-24": {
      "scriptHash": "6dc8f40a2a097bca61a2cac77484a1c1c0ecaaddb44c981d186af8de5cabe786",
      "sigVersion": 3,
      "bytes": 573902,
      "durationSec": 35.81,
      "audioSha256": "e4ab979b9111a9287c186605bf7b916c25ba64d7dd50455ec96ad27a10c56000",
      "stt": {
        "verdict": "PASS",
        "wer": 0.0,
        "backend": "faster_whisper",
        "reason": "WER 0.0%",
        "transcript": "Good afternoon, students. This is a quick reminder about the updated entry requirements for the North Campus Fitness Center starting this Monday. To improve security, the old plastic membership cards will no longer be accepted at the turnstiles. Instead, all students must now scan the digital QR code available through the University Life mobile app to gain access. If you haven't downloaded the app yet, please do so before your next workout to avoid any delays at the entrance. For a step-by-step guide on how to set up your digital ID, please visit the help desk in the main lobby or check the official athletics department website.",
        "audioSha256": "e4ab979b9111a9287c186605bf7b916c25ba64d7dd50455ec96ad27a10c56000",
        "scriptHash": "6dc8f40a2a097bca61a2cac77484a1c1c0ecaaddb44c981d186af8de5cabe786"
      }
    },
    "set2-l1-q25-28": {
      "scriptHash": "8f55c1f691db908e298c6a076f1b580d47e74d67e46e8cc5a26cf0d4558e27d6",
      "sigVersion": 3,
      "bytes": 1559867,
      "durationSec": 97.43,
      "audioSha256": "fec0141052e2937a5224283a2809e1369e326c0f98f99854e3fd7e4582a8740e",
      "stt": {
        "verdict": "PASS",
        "wer": 0.0,
        "backend": "faster_whisper",
        "reason": "WER 0.0%",
        "transcript": "So today, let's talk about something called brand loyalty. Basically, brand loyalty is when customers keep buying the same brand over and over again, even when there are other options available. You know, like when someone always buys the same type of phone or always goes to the same coffee shop. Now, why does this happen? Well, there are a few key reasons. First, consistency plays a big role. When a product or service delivers the same quality every time, customers start to trust it. I mean, if your favorite restaurant always makes great food, you're more likely to go back, right? Second, emotional connection matters. Companies create this through advertising, customer service, or even just memories. Think about a brand your family has used for years. There's often an emotional attachment there. However, brand loyalty isn't permanent. If quality drops, or if a competitor offers something significantly better, customers might switch. Also, younger consumers tend to be less loyal than older generations, because they value trying new things. That said, strong brand loyalty is incredibly valuable for businesses. It reduces marketing costs, since loyal customers basically advertise for you through word of mouth. Plus, these customers are often willing to pay premium prices.",
        "audioSha256": "fec0141052e2937a5224283a2809e1369e326c0f98f99854e3fd7e4582a8740e",
        "scriptHash": "8f55c1f691db908e298c6a076f1b580d47e74d67e46e8cc5a26cf0d4558e27d6"
      }
    },
    "set2-l1-q29-32": {
      "scriptHash": "60acfeffc94657d2426209059b568aca348a974ea7f4f1a913e25062ad93ef64",
      "sigVersion": 3,
      "bytes": 1403968,
      "durationSec": 87.68,
      "audioSha256": "d6dfa7489d34457813642da0ef3b79836cef264eb113d8f951997226fd9d1578",
      "stt": {
        "verdict": "PASS",
        "wer": 0.0092,
        "backend": "faster_whisper",
        "reason": "WER 0.9%",
        "transcript": "In many ecosystems, we see species that look nearly identical when they live in separate geographic areas. But when these same two species overlap in the same habitat, they often start to diverge. This phenomenon is a direct response to the intense pressure of resource competition. If two species require the exact same food source in the same place, one will eventually out-compete the other, potentially leading to local extinction. To avoid this, we observe what ecologists call character displacement. Character displacement refers to the evolutionary process where two similar species develop distinct physical differences, specifically to minimize competition. Essentially, it's a way for species to carve out separate ecological niches within the shared territory. Instead of competing for the identical food types, they adapt to utilize different parts of the environment. Look at how this works with certain bird populations like Darwin's finches. On islands where only one species lives, their beak sizes are usually intermediate. However, on islands where two species coexist, their beak sizes shift dramatically. One species evolves a larger beak for tough seeds, while the other develops a smaller one for smaller food items. This divergence ensures that neither species is in direct competition for the same specific resource, allowing both to thrive. It's a crucial mechanism for maintaining biodiversity in competitive environments.",
        "audioSha256": "d6dfa7489d34457813642da0ef3b79836cef264eb113d8f951997226fd9d1578",
        "scriptHash": "60acfeffc94657d2426209059b568aca348a974ea7f4f1a913e25062ad93ef64"
      }
    },
